Contract: `StartSampler` records on the requested interval until `ctx` is canceled, then releases its timer resources. This service runs under Go 1.22. The code is:

```go
func StartSampler(ctx context.Context, every time.Duration, record func(time.Time)) {
    go func() {
        for {
            select {
            case <-ctx.Done():
                return
            case t := <-time.Tick(every):
                record(t)
            }
        }
    }()
}
```

Does this meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.
